#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:1
msgid "Responsible AI integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:3
msgid ""
"The Open Data Editor (ODE) has an AI component to help users better "
"understand their data. The AI component is powered by local models. **No "
"data is sent to the cloud, and all operations take place on the user’s "
"computer.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:5
msgid ""
"The introduction of these AI-assisted data quality features significantly"
" expands the tool’s capabilities, enabling faster identification of "
"anomalies, smarter suggestions for corrections, and improved handling of "
"large, dense datasets while retaining a privacy-preserving, local-first "
"design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:7
msgid ""
"This deepens Open Knowledge Foundation's commitment to developing simple,"
" sustainable and long-lasting technologies that solve people’s real "
"problems, in line with [The Tech We Want](https://okfn.org/en/projects"
"/the-tech-we-want/) initiative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:9
msgid ""
"In order to use the AI feature, ODE will guide users to download the "
"model onto their machine first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:12
msgid ""
"As the model is local and all computing will be happening in the user’s "
"computer, performance will be affected by the machine’s hardware, and the"
" response quality sometimes will be minor than typical cloud LLMs like "
"ChatGPT, Deepseek or Claude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/responsible-ai-integration.md:15
msgid ""
"ODE is trying to balance user experience for non-technical audiences and "
"performance and privacy."
msgstr ""

